---
layout: layouts/page.njk
title: IT Training
description: "Structured programs in web development, QA, cloud, and data — built for graduates who want training that leads somewhere specific: a job."
extraScripts:
  - /assets/js/faq-accordion.js
  - /assets/js/rail-active.js
---
{% from "partials/icons.njk" import icon %}

{#
  This page assumes the four tracks in _data/programs.json are real, with real curricula
  and instructors. If they are not, it ships the waitlist version instead — no durations,
  no prices, no curriculum until they exist. See CONTENT.md §8.

  Never "guaranteed placement" anywhere on this page. Always "direct" or "priority
  access" to the placement pipeline.
#}

{% set rail = [
  { id: "programs",   label: "Tracks offered", n: "00" },
  { id: "why",        label: "Why train here", n: "A"  },
  { id: "credential", label: "What you get",   n: "B"  },
  { id: "pricing",    label: "Pricing",        n: "C"  },
  { id: "procedure",  label: "Curriculum",     n: "D"  },
  { id: "faq",        label: "Questions",      n: "E"  }
] %}

{% set crumbs = [{ label: "Home", url: "/" }, { label: "Services", url: "/services/" }, { label: "IT Training" }] %}
{% set coverStamp = "File · 05" %}
{% set coverTitle = "Train. Certify. Get placed." %}
{% set coverLead = "Structured programs that build real skills — and feed straight into our placement pipeline when you're done." %}
{% set coverPrimary = { label: "Book a Free Demo Class", href: "/contact/?role=training" } %}
{% set coverSecondary = { label: "See job placement", href: "/services/job-placement/" } %}
{% set coverImage = images.services["it-training"].cover %}
{% include "partials/cover-sheet.njk" %}

<section class="section-container py-14 sm:py-20">
  <div class="lg:grid lg:grid-cols-12 lg:gap-12">

    {% include "partials/section-rail.njk" %}

    <div class="lg:col-span-9">

      {# ---- 00 Tracks. Duration, format and prerequisites are the three things a
             learner filters on first, so they are on the card, not in the FAQ. ---- #}
      <div id="programs" class="scroll-mt-28">
        <p class="eyebrow">00 — Programs</p>
        <h2 class="mt-2 max-w-xl font-display text-2xl font-semibold leading-tight tracking-tight text-ink sm:text-3xl">
          Tracks offered.
        </h2>
        {# Each track is a full panel rather than a card in a grid: a learner comparing
           programs wants curriculum, format and prerequisites side by side, and four
           cramped tiles cannot carry that. Images alternate side to keep the run from
           reading as a list. #}
        <div class="mt-6 space-y-5">
          {% for program in programs.list %}
          {% set shot = images.services["it-training"].tracks[program.title] %}
          {# !pt-0 because folder-card's top padding would otherwise print a strip of
             paper above the image; the text cell carries its own padding instead. #}
          <article class="folder-card overflow-hidden !pt-0 md:grid md:grid-cols-12">
            {% if shot %}
            <img src="{{ shot.url }}" alt="{{ shot.alt }}" width="{{ shot.width }}" height="{{ shot.height }}"
                 loading="lazy"
                 class="h-44 w-full object-cover md:col-span-4 md:h-full {% if loop.index is even %}md:order-last{% endif %}">
            {% endif %}
            <div class="p-5 {% if shot %}md:col-span-8{% else %}md:col-span-12{% endif %}">
              <div class="flex items-start justify-between gap-3">
                <span class="flex h-9 w-9 items-center justify-center rounded-sm bg-brand/10 text-brand">{{ icon(program.icon, "w-4 h-4") }}</span>
                {# A duration is metadata, not a file number — so it stays in ink, not vermilion. #}
                <span class="meta">{{ program.duration }}</span>
              </div>
              <h3 class="mt-3 font-display text-xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-ink">{{ program.title }}</h3>
              <p class="mt-2 body-copy">{{ program.description }}</p>
              <dl class="mt-4 grid grid-cols-2 gap-4 border-t border-dashed border-border pt-4">
                <div class="flex flex-col-reverse">
                  <dt class="mt-1 meta">Format</dt>
                  <dd class="text-sm font-medium text-ink">{{ program.format }}</dd>
                </div>
                <div class="flex flex-col-reverse">
                  <dt class="mt-1 meta">Prerequisites</dt>
                  <dd class="text-sm font-medium text-ink">{{ program.prerequisites }}</dd>
                </div>
              </dl>
            </div>
          </article>
          {% endfor %}
        </div>
      </div>

      {# ---- A The differentiator against a generic training vendor. ---- #}
      <div id="why" class="mt-14 scroll-mt-28">
        <p class="eyebrow">A — Why train with us</p>
        <p class="statement mt-4 !text-ink sm:!text-2xl">
          Graduates get <span class="text-brand">direct access to our placement pipeline</span> — the file is already open on the day you certify.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-6 max-w-xl text-lg leading-relaxed text-ink/75">
          That's priority access, not a guarantee. It's the difference between an open application and a recruiter who already knows your work.
        </p>
      </div>

      {# ---- B What certification actually means. Vague certification claims are the
             most common complaint about training providers. ---- #}
      <div id="credential" class="mt-14 scroll-mt-28">
        <p class="eyebrow">B — At the end</p>
        <h2 class="mt-2 max-w-xl font-display text-2xl font-semibold leading-tight tracking-tight text-ink sm:text-3xl">
          What you get at the end.
        </h2>
        <div class="mt-6 grid grid-cols-1 gap-5 sm:grid-cols-3">
          {% set outcomes = [
            { icon: "check-badge", t: "A completion certificate", d: "Issued by " + site.companyName + ", naming the track and the hours behind it." },
            { icon: "code", t: "A portfolio project", d: "Something you can show an employer, not a printable PDF." },
            { icon: "briefcase", t: "A handoff to placement", d: "A direct introduction into our Job Placement pipeline." }
          ] %}
          {% for item in outcomes %}
          <div class="folder-card p-5">
            <span class="flex h-9 w-9 items-center justify-center rounded-sm bg-brand/10 text-brand">{{ icon(item.icon, "w-4 h-4") }}</span>
            <h3 class="mt-3 font-display font-semibold tracking-tight text-ink">{{ item.t }}</h3>
            <p class="mt-2 body-copy">{{ item.d }}</p>
          </div>
          {% endfor %}
        </div>
        <p class="mt-5 file-inset meta leading-relaxed">
          Where a track prepares you for a vendor exam, we say which one and whether the exam fee is included — ask us for the track you're considering.
        </p>
      </div>

      {# ---- C Pricing. A page with no price signal loses price-sensitive readers
             entirely, so at minimum state that plans exist and how to get figures. ---- #}
      <div id="pricing" class="mt-14 scroll-mt-28">
        <p class="eyebrow">C — Pricing</p>
        <h2 class="mt-2 max-w-xl font-display text-2xl font-semibold leading-tight tracking-tight text-ink sm:text-3xl">
          What it costs.
        </h2>
        <p class="mt-4 max-w-xl text-lg leading-relaxed text-ink/75">
          Program fees vary by track and format. Payment plans are available, and select tracks offer a placement-linked deferral.
        </p>
        <a href="{{ '/contact/?role=training' | url }}" class="mt-5 inline-flex items-center gap-2 font-semibold text-brand transition-all hover:gap-3">
          Tell us your track and we'll send exact pricing {{ icon("arrow-right", "w-4 h-4") }}
        </a>
      </div>

      {# ---- D Curriculum. The clearest literal run of the pipeline: it ends at the
             same Job Placement file. ---- #}
      <div class="mt-14">
        {% set steps = [
          { label: "Enroll", description: "Pick a track and a format — online, in-person, or both." },
          { label: "Learn", description: "Structured curriculum built around real job requirements." },
          { label: "Practice", description: "A portfolio-ready project you can show employers." },
          { label: "Certification", description: "A credential that signals real, tested skill." },
          { label: "Placement support", description: "Direct handoff into our Job Placement pipeline." }
        ] %}
        {% set sectionId = "procedure" %}
        {% set sectionEyebrow = "D — Curriculum" %}
        {% set sectionTitle = "From enrollment to placement." %}
        {% include "partials/process-timeline.njk" %}
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

{% set faqKey = "it-training" %}
{% set faqEyebrow = "E — Standing questions" %}
{% set faqTitle = "Before you enroll." %}
{% include "partials/faq-accordion.njk" %}

{% set ctaStamp = "Ready to open" %}
{% set ctaHeadline = "Ready to build a new skill set?" %}
{% set ctaSubtext = "Sit in on a demo class first — there's no cost and no commitment." %}
{% set ctaLabel = "Enroll Now" %}
{% set ctaHref = "/contact/?role=training" %}
{% include "partials/cta-section.njk" %}
